WEBVTT

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:28.735
The Coverup Beneath the AI Hacking Scandals, from Effort. Subtitle: AI cyberattacks were caused by nepotistic contracting, not rogue AI.

00:00:29.385 --> 00:00:43.835
Last quarter's AI cyberattacks are a classic human problem. Not only were the cyberattacks caused by human errors, building a faulty sandbox and instructing the AI models to act, they reflect one of Silicon Valley's oldest growing pains.

00:00:44.485 --> 00:01:02.035
Anthropic has tried and failed to hire "independent" auditors in the wake of committing several cyberattacks with its commercial partner, Irregular. Instead, it has repeatedly hired ideologically homogeneous "Effective Altruist" organizations with no cybersecurity experience.

00:01:02.685 --> 00:01:17.010
The reason for their failure is a systemic pattern of corrupt hiring and contracting by E A employees. This will lead to more cyberattacks unless Anthropic and other AI companies combat this pattern of self-preferential hiring.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:34.595
Effort analyzed two hundred ninety-three AI company hiring relationships and found a consistent pattern of nepotism: Effective Altruist program participants hire each other at much higher rates than non-E As.

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:44.070
This likely understates the rate of ingroup bias, since it does not count Effective Altruist ideologues who did not participate in official E A programs.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:02:04.870
Leaders from E A programs hired forty-one point one percent subordinates with E A programs, compared to twenty-six point two percent for employers with no E A program history. Employees from E A programs have E A leaders twenty-seven point one percent of the time, as opposed to fifteen point nine percent for employees with no E A program history.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:19.920
This is a classic Silicon Valley problem: when startups make it big, they shed many early ideologues who believed in the technology first in exchange for more seasoned professionals. True believers with enough competence can survive this transition.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:45.305
Across the past three months, employees of OpenAI, Anthropic, or their business partner Irregular instructed their respective AI models to commit cyberattacks. Then, those models committed cyberattacks in the real world. These companies claim that they accidentally gave these AI models internet access, leading them to attack real world targets.

00:02:45.955 --> 00:03:02.630
In the wake of these cyberattacks, OpenAI, Anthropic, Irregular, and their media allies insisted on a "rogue agent" narrative. In their telling, "misaligned" models "schemed" to "go rogue" and "become threat actors". In reality, the models followed the instructions of their creators.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:19.555
Zack Korman, a cybersecurity founder and self-described ex-doomer, explained the issue with this argument. "The biggest problem with this E A-helping-E A network is the extent to which these firms really are not the best at all, but rather just happen to share this affiliation."

00:03:20.205 --> 00:03:31.055
In a June twenty twenty-five interview, Anthropic president Daniela Amodei described a "very extreme almost emphasis on ensuring cultural alignment in your early employees."

00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:42.965
The clearest case of this nepotistic behavior is the culprit behind the majority of the cyberattacks: Irregular.

00:03:43.615 --> 00:04:02.190
Irregular's founders have documented organizational and funding ties to E A. C E O Dan Lahav and Sella Nevo were the joint named recipients of a three hundred ninety-four thousand, nine hundred sixty-eight dollar E A Infrastructure Fund grant recommendation in twenty twenty-two for an online course.

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:16.665
Lahav and Sella co-founded Impact Focused Education. C T O Omer Nevo and Sella co-founded Probably Good and serve on its board; Omer also advises Heron, an E A Israel project funded by Coefficient Giving.

00:04:16.665 --> 00:04:34.965
Good Ventures, the foundation created by Dustin Moskovitz and Cari Tuna, paid Irregular six point eight million dollars across two grant installments in twenty twenty-four and twenty twenty-five. Its filings separately listed a three million dollar stock holding in Pattern Labs Tech Inc., Irregular's legal name.

00:04:35.615 --> 00:04:46.565
Effective Altruist ideologues like Irregular were responsible for the majority of AI hacking incidents. We asked Korman to explain the Effective Altruism hiring network.

00:04:46.565 --> 00:05:04.640
"They can all support each other and make statements that lead the public to believe something, for example that METR is some elite investigation unit, when really it's just one network propping each other up. That is extremely powerful, but it's not good when it is playing such a central role in policy discussions."

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:19.975
Some companies are taking steps towards professionalizing. OpenAI has expanded its partnership with CrowdStrike, one of the largest traditional cybersecurity providers.

00:05:19.975 --> 00:05:41.475
Meanwhile, OpenAI fired several of its "AI Safety" employees surrounding the Hugging Face attack and other cyberattacks because "they violated clear policies on handling sensitive information." Another risk of Effective Altruist employees is the illegal sharing of sensitive information, particularly with OpenAI's competitor, Anthropic.

00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:55.900
Simultaneously, Anthropic received backlash for doubling down on Effective Altruist firms. Anthropic prioritized METR, whose founders had little cybersecurity experience, over non-E A firms with experience.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:05.800
Irregular, the firm responsible for providing the models with internet access and building the cybersecurity environments, is another example of E A nepotism.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:21.750
Anthropic designated Faculty, an E A firm acquired by Accenture, an evaluator; meanwhile, Faculty founder Marc Warner organized an "AI Safety" conference with the British king to push E A ideology and indirectly push Anthropic's business interest.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:43.535
Effective Altruists justify nepotistic hiring using a number of circular, E A-funded credentials. The problem is that these credentials form a Potemkin village of false expertise, consisting more of sermons about the end of the world than practical cybersecurity training.

00:06:43.535 --> 00:06:59.285
"If a bunch of E A people want to do that in an area that doesn't matter then who cares, but suddenly we are seeing legislative calls to basically codify some of this work into law. And I think then these connections need to be a lot more transparent," Korman told Effort.

00:06:59.935 --> 00:07:19.860
By contracting with his ideological allies, Dario also boosts their legitimacy in the eyes of other AI companies, who may not realize that they were hired for ideological alignment. In the case of Irregular, Google, OpenAI, and Meta also contracted with them, making them a central point of failure for all four companies' cyberattacks.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:26.060
As awareness of Anthropic's hiring and contracting priorities spreads, this may change rapidly.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:33.035
We asked conservative policy scholar Will Thibeau how policymakers should think about these cyberattacks.

00:07:33.035 --> 00:07:47.935
"In a world where such bias is so evident and clear, policy makers should ensure the preservation and flourishing of open weight and open source models that make up for the risk of ideological with transparency and insight into model construction."

00:07:52.545 --> 00:08:05.820
Ultimately, there is nothing new under the sun. OpenAI and Anthropic face the same human growing pains as every other Silicon Valley company, and it is a sign of their success that they face this scrutiny in the first place.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:20.945
However, the time-tested solution is to terminate nepotistically hired contractors and employees, as OpenAI is naturally beginning to do, not to double down on them. In reality, the rogue agents are not the AIs, but the Effective Altruists.

00:08:21.595 --> 00:08:25.070
The sources and study data section was skipped.
